{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "34268400-9818-43c5-96db-7110e14ede09",
    "name": "Activity5-CTADWEBL",
    "description": "Laboratory Activity 5 (Custom Middleware and API Security) - tests the audit logger, input validation, Helmet/CORS headers, and rate limiting (including the escalating login lockout) for the BulldogEx Shop API.\n\n1. Start the server first: npm run dev (inside marzan-server), and run npm run seed at least once so admin@bulldogex.nu.edu.ph exists.\n2. Send the requests from top to bottom; tokens and ids are saved into collection variables as you go.\n3. Requests marked [Validation] are supposed to fail; their tests pass when the API rejects the request as expected.\n4. Folder 4 deliberately fails 5 logins in a row to trigger the escalating lockout (Part 9) - this is expected and intentional.\n\nFolder 5 deletes the temporary customer (Grace) this collection created.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
